text.section:
A corporation restating its articles of incorporation shall file with the Commission articles of restatement setting forth:

The name of the corporation immediately prior to restatement;


Whether the restatement contains a new amendment to the articles;


The text of the restated articles of incorporation or amended and restated articles of incorporation, as the case may be;


Information required by subdivision L 5 of § 13.1-804;


The date of the restatement's adoption;


If the restatement does not contain a new amendment to the articles, that the board of directors adopted the restatement;


If the restatement contains a new amendment to the articles not requiring member approval, the information required by subdivision A 4 of § 13.1-888; and


If the restatement contains a new amendment to the articles requiring member approval, the information required by subdivision A 5 of § 13.1-888.
